\begin{abstract}
Apex-TI is a fully software-defined quantum--topological simulation framework
capable of modeling multi-scale physical phenomena without hardware constraints.
The system integrates autonomous solver intelligence, distributed tensor fabrics,
compiler-optimized sparse kernels, and a virtual quantum substrate (VQS) that
supports synthetic physics constants and deterministic time-reversal replay.
This paper presents the architecture, mathematical foundations, and stress-testing
protocols validating the numerical stability and topological invariant preservation
of Apex-TI v4.0.
\end{abstract}

\section{Introduction}
The Apex-TI framework provides a substrate-agnostic environment for simulating
quantum and topological systems entirely in software. Unlike hardware-bound
approaches, Apex-TI leverages distributed memory fabrics and autonomous numerical
solvers to maintain stability under extreme spectral, non-Markovian, and defect-
driven stress conditions.

