\section{Mathematical Foundations}
The virtual Hamiltonian is constructed as:
\[
H_{ij} = t_{ij} + \rho_d f(i,j) + \eta g(i,j),
\]
where $t_{ij}$ encodes hopping amplitudes, $\rho_d$ controls defect density,
and $\eta$ introduces spectral perturbation.

The solver monitors the condition number:
\[
\kappa = \frac{\sigma_{\max}}{\sigma_{\min}},
\]
triggering autonomous preconditioning when $\kappa > 10^{10}$.

